 "final_message": "All 11 work items are done, and the test suite passes (6 tests, including the two new ones).\n\n- **Code (items 1\u20138):**\n  - `monitor_flag_rate` and `pooled_flag_rate` now return `0.0` when there are no transcripts. Only a `flagged` value of `True` counts as flagged. The pooled rate divides total flags by total transcripts instead of averaging group rates.\n  - `flags_in_window` sums the last `days` entries, and returns `0` when `days` is 0.\n  - `parse_transcript_log` skips blank lines, whitespace-only lines and `#` lines. It strips whitespace around each field and reads `flagged` as `1` for True, `0` for False and empty for None. Previously any non-empty value, including `0`, parsed as True.\n  - `dedupe_transcripts` keeps the last record for each id.\n  - `daily_flag_counts` returns one entry per day from `start_day` to `end_day`, with zeros for empty days, and ignores transcripts outside the range.\n  - `monitor_summary` rounds `rate` to 3 places and counts only groups that have at least one transcript.\n- **Tests (items 9\u201310):** I added a test for `None` counting as not flagged, which also checks the empty-list rate. I also added one for `dedupe_transcripts` keeping the last duplicate id.\n- **README (item 11):** I fixed the `flags_in_window` entry and added a `daily_flag_counts` entry. I also reworded the `dedupe_transcripts` entry, which you didn't ask for, so it states the keep-last rule and the sort order.",
